---
// /companies — the waiting list for a company page.
//
// What a company gets is described concretely, because the alternative is the
// thing this site exists against: a vague promise of exposure, sold. There is
// nothing to buy here. Placement is never sold, and there is no ranking to
// rank in.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import BeforeYouRely from '../components/BeforeYouRely.astro';
import WaitlistForm from '../components/WaitlistForm.astro';
import { ORG_NAME, SITE_URL, abs } from '../lib/site';
import { US_STATES, NO_FEE_LINE, NEVER_SOLD_LINE } from '../lib/waitlist';

const path = '/companies';
const title = `Company waiting list — a page for your chimney company | ${ORG_NAME}`;
const description =
  'Join the waiting list for a company page on Chimney.Services: services, service area, contacts and certified people, each fact labeled. No fee, no ranking.';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: ORG_NAME, item: SITE_URL },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Company waiting list' },
    ],
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    '@id': `${abs(path)}#page`,
    url: abs(path),
    name: title,
    description,
    isPartOf: { '@id': `${SITE_URL}/#organization` },
    publisher: { '@id': `${SITE_URL}/#organization` },
    about: {
      '@type': 'Thing',
      name: 'Chimney company pages on Chimney.Services',
      description:
        'A provenance-labeled summary of what a chimney company says it does and what public record shows, which the company can correct and cannot buy.',
    },
  },
];
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path={path} jsonLd={jsonLd} section="companies">
  <nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">CHIMNEY.SERVICES / COMPANY WAITING LIST</nav>

  <div class="wl-page">
    <h1>Company waiting list — a page for your chimney company, every fact labeled</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      We are building one page per chimney company, in the same shape for every company, with a label on every fact
      saying where it came from. This is the queue to have yours built. It costs nothing, and nothing about it is for
      sale.
    </p>

    <section class="wl-section" aria-labelledby="join-h" id="join">
      <h2 id="join-h">Join the waiting list</h2>
      <p>
        Seven fields, five of them required. We write to you once, when company pages open in your state.
      </p>

      <WaitlistForm
        type="company"
        id="company-waitlist"
        opensLabel="company pages"
        button="Join the waiting list"
        fieldsClass="wl-fields--two"
      >
          <p class="wl-field wl-field--wide">
            <label for="wl-company">Company name<span class="wl-req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
            <input id="wl-company" name="company" type="text" required maxlength="120" autocomplete="organization" />
          </p>
          <p class="wl-field">
            <label for="wl-contact">Your name<span class="wl-req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
            <input id="wl-contact" name="contact" type="text" required maxlength="120" autocomplete="name" />
          </p>
          <p class="wl-field">
            <label for="wl-email">Email<span class="wl-req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
            <input id="wl-email" name="email" type="email" required maxlength="160" autocomplete="email" />
          </p>
          <p class="wl-field">
            <label for="wl-phone">Phone <span class="wl-opt">(optional)</span></label>
            <input id="wl-phone" name="phone" type="tel" maxlength="40" autocomplete="tel" />
          </p>
          <p class="wl-field">
            <label for="wl-state">State<span class="wl-req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
            <select id="wl-state" name="state" required>
              <option value="">Choose a state</option>
              {US_STATES.map((s) => <option value={s.abbr}>{s.name}</option>)}
            </select>
          </p>
          <p class="wl-field">
            <label for="wl-city">City<span class="wl-req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
            <input id="wl-city" name="city" type="text" required maxlength="80" autocomplete="address-level2" />
          </p>
          <p class="wl-field wl-field--wide">
            <label for="wl-website">Website <span class="wl-opt">(optional)</span></label>
            <input id="wl-website" name="website" type="text" maxlength="200" inputmode="url" placeholder="example.com" />
          </p>
      </WaitlistForm>

      <p class="fineprint">{NO_FEE_LINE}</p>
    </section>

    <section class="wl-section" aria-labelledby="what-h" id="what-you-get">
      <h2 id="what-h">What are you waiting for, exactly?</h2>
      <p>
        A page like <a href="/chicago">the one we built for Chimney Monkey</a> — read it first, then decide whether you
        want one. Every block on it carries one of two labels: <strong>PUBLIC RECORD</strong> for something taken from a
        public source we name, or <strong>REPORTED BY BUSINESS</strong> for something the company itself says. The page
        holds:
      </p>
      <ul class="wl-list">
        <li>
          <span class="wl-list__label">Services</span>
          What the company says it does, grouped for reading, taken from its own pages and labeled as the company's own
          words. Nothing on that list has been watched, tested or priced by us.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="wl-list__label">Service area</span>
          The counties and towns the company names itself. A town on that list is a place a company says it goes, not a
          promise that it will.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="wl-list__label">Contacts and hours</span>
          Address, phone, email, website and opening hours, each labeled with where we found it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="wl-list__label">Certified people</span>
          Anyone at the company found on a certification body's own public roster, with the date we looked. Bodies are
          always in the same order — NCSG, then NFI, then CSIA, then any other body — so what is missing is as visible
          as what is there.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="wl-list__label">Google rating</span>
          The rating and review count as Google Maps displayed them on the day we looked, dated, with the plain caveat
          that we did not read the reviews and both numbers will have moved since. We publish no rating markup anywhere.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You can correct any of it. Send us what is wrong and what the right answer is, and the page changes or the page
        says you disagree. What you cannot do is buy your way onto it, or up it. {NEVER_SOLD_LINE}
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="wl-section" aria-labelledby="not-h" id="what-it-is-not">
      <h2 id="not-h">What a company page is not</h2>
      <ul class="prose">
        <li>It is not an endorsement. We recommend no one, and we never will.</li>
        <li>
          It is not a rank. There is no order to climb, no badge to earn, and no position that money moves. A company
          page is a record of dated facts with their sources named.
        </li>
        <li>
          It is not a check on the company. We do not inspect work, call customers, read complaint histories, or confirm
          insurance. Where a certification is shown, the claim is only that a body's own public roster showed that name
          on the date printed beside it.
        </li>
        <li>
          It is not an advertisement, and nothing on it is sold. We take no fee from any certification body, guild, or
          contractor, and nobody is paid to be mentioned.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <BeforeYouRely variant="waitlist" />

    <p class="wl-crosslink">
      Are you a chimney technician rather than an owner? <a href="/professionals">Join the waiting list for a record
      and an ID card of your own</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
